  "note": "ALA-LC Georgian Romanization Table, 2011 version, pp. 1-2 (Khutsuri upper/lower columns with romanization; Mkhedruli column not transcribed for this map); held source interscript-private-references/alalc/alalc-georgian.pdf. Extraction: PDF text layer, every value cell cross-checked against the rendered page image. Aspirated/ejective values use the modifier turned comma (ʻ, U+02BB): Tʻ, Pʻ, Kʻ, Čʻ, Cʻ and their lower cases, transcribed as printed. The table prints Khutsuri upper case, Khutsuri lower case and Mkhedruli side by side; this map (Geok = Khutsuri) takes the Khutsuri columns only. The Mkhedruli column pairs 1:1 with the Khutsuri lower case in the grid (aside from the four tail letters), so the lower-case rows double as the Mkhedruli values. Skipped printed rows: ჶ (f), ჷ (ĕ), ჸ (ʻ ayn), უ̌/უ̂ (ŭ) — Mkhedruli-only tail rows of the printed table with no Khutsuri letter: they belong to the Mkhedruli map, not this Khutsuri (Geok) map; skipped here."
